# motorfader: the TOGGLE TRICK (issue #45) — `button = _T` + `clear = _T` on one
# fader, wired back into `startvalue`, turns the touch plate into a toggle. The
# Forge's MFPS generator uses exactly this shape for the clock mute:
#
#     output     = _V
#     button     = _T          # plate press
#     clear      = _T          # ...re-seeds startvalue
#     startvalue = -1 * _V + 1 # ...to the INVERSE of the current value
#
# The recall must STAY. On hardware the motor is disabled while a finger is on
# the fader/plate, so the fader does not physically follow the recall until the
# hand comes off — yet the virtual value is the recalled one from the recall tick
# onward. vcvoid's panel echoes the (unchanged) physical position into the engine
# every frame while the fader counts as held (plugin/src/MasterBase.hpp feeds
# moveFader under the touch gate), which is what `move F1 <same position>` below
# models: that echo must NOT overwrite the recall.
#
#   @0    boots at dent 1 (startvalue = -1 * 0 + 1)
#   @1    plate down -> _T high
#   @2    clear fires -> recall to dent 0
#   @3-4  panel keeps echoing the stale (pre-recall) position while held -> stays 0
#   @6    plate released, the motor has moved the fader; the panel catches up
#   @7-10 second press toggles back to dent 1 and stays there
tickrate 100
patch <<<
[m4]

[motorfader]
    fader      = 1
    notches    = 2
    output     = _V
    button     = _T
    clear      = _T
    startvalue = -1 * _V + 1

[copy]
    input  = _V
    output = O1
>>>
@0 expect O1 1 tol 1e-4
@0 expect F1 1 tol 1e-4
# --- first press: toggle 1 -> 0 -------------------------------------------
@1 touch F1 1
@1 move F1 1
@1 expect O1 1 tol 1e-4
@2 move F1 1
@2 expect O1 0 tol 1e-4
@2 expect F1 0 tol 1e-4
# the plate is still held: the stale physical position must not win it back
@3 move F1 1
@3 expect O1 0 tol 1e-4
@4 move F1 1
@4 expect O1 0 tol 1e-4
@5 touch F1 0
@5 expect O1 0 tol 1e-4
# released: the motor has taken the fader to the recalled dent, the panel echo
# now reports that position -- still 0, and the hold is over
@6 move F1 0
@6 expect O1 0 tol 1e-4
# --- second press: toggle 0 -> 1 ------------------------------------------
@7 touch F1 1
@7 move F1 0
@7 expect O1 0 tol 1e-4
@8 move F1 0
@8 expect O1 1 tol 1e-4
@8 expect F1 1 tol 1e-4
@9 move F1 0
@9 expect O1 1 tol 1e-4
@10 move F1 0
@10 expect O1 1 tol 1e-4
@11 touch F1 0
@12 expect O1 1 tol 1e-4
